## Design Tokens

All tokens are read from the CSS cascade. No values are hard-coded.

| Property      | CSS Custom Property                                | Source                          |
| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Section gap   | `var(--AreaChart-gap, var(--Spacing-5))`           | `AreaChart.module.css`          |
| Series color 1| `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-1)`                | `generateDataVisCSS` output     |
| Series color 2| `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-2)`                | `generateDataVisCSS` output     |
| Series color N| `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-N)`                | `generateDataVisCSS` output     |

The `--AreaChart-gap` hook is the consumer/brand override. When absent, it falls back to `--Spacing-5` from the OneUI cascade.

## Legend Auto-Generation

When `chartLegendConfig.items` is not provided, the chart derives legend items from `detectedSeriesInfo` (unique series found in `data`):

1. Each series becomes one legend item with `type: 'circle'`
2. `series.name` maps to `categoryLabelValue`
3. `series.color` is used if set; otherwise `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-${index + 1})` is assigned
4. The order follows `seriesOrder` (if provided) or the natural order in the data

```tsx
// Auto-generated with categorical colors from DataVis cascade
<AreaChart
  data={data}
  chartLegend
  seriesOrder={['Revenue', 'Expenses']}
/>
```

## Stacking Behavior

| Mode           | D3 Offset              | Description                                                                  |
| -------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `'stacked'`    | `d3.stackOffsetNone`   | Areas accumulate — top edge is the cumulative total (default)                |
| `'layered'`    | Manual baseline at 0   | Every series starts at zero and overlaps — compare absolute magnitudes       |
| `'fullHeight'` | `d3.stackOffsetExpand` | Normalised to 100% at every category — market share / part-to-whole          |

`'fullHeight'` mode disables the broken-axis feature (`skippedTicks`) since the domain is always 0–1. Negative values are not supported in this mode.

### Stacked arithmetic example

```
series: [
  { values: [10, 20, 30] },  // Series 1 — bottom
  { values: [15, 25, 35] },  // Series 2
  { values: [5,  10, 15] },  // Series 3 — top
]

Stacked y-values:
  Series 1: [0–10],   [0–20],   [0–30]
  Series 2: [10–25],  [20–45],  [30–65]
  Series 3: [25–30],  [45–55],  [65–80]
```

## Height Behavior

`height` is the **total container height**. AreaGroup fills remaining vertical space after header, legend, DataDisplay, and footer.

```
┌───────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ChartHeader (title + subtitle)       │  ← auto height
├───────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ChartLegend (optional)               │  ← auto height
├───────────────────────────────────────┤
│  DataDisplay (optional)               │  ← auto height
├───────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                       │
│            AreaGroup                  │  ← flex: 1 (fills remaining)
│     (YAxis + Areas + XAxis)           │
│                                       │
├───────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ChartFooter (source + notes)         │  ← auto height
└───────────────────────────────────────┘
        Total height: `height` prop
```

AreaGroup receives `height="100%"` and uses `ResizeObserver` to measure actual pixel height for D3 scaling.

## Hover Interaction

When `interactive={true}` (default), hovering a series highlights it while dimming others. The `onSeriesHover` callback in `areaGroupConfig` fires with an `AreaSeriesHoverData` object:

```typescript
interface AreaSeriesHoverData {
  seriesIndex: number;
  name?: string;
  isHovered: boolean;
  category?: string;
  categoryValues?: { name: string; value: number }[];
}
```

## Accessibility

The chart is wrapped by `ChartAccessibility`:

- `role="figure"` with `aria-label` (defaults to chart title)
- `aria-describedby` pointing to a visually-hidden `<table>` with all data points
- `aria-live="polite"` region for hover/focus announcements
- All decorative SVG elements carry `aria-hidden="true"`

### Keyboard Navigation

| Key               | Action                                        |
| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| `Tab`             | Focus the chart data-point group (one stop)   |
| `ArrowRight`      | Next category                                 |
| `ArrowLeft`       | Previous category                             |
| `Home`            | First category                                |
| `End`             | Last category                                 |
| `Enter` / `Space` | Activate focused data point                   |

Each category renders an invisible focusable slice with `role="button"`, `aria-roledescription="data point"`, and an `aria-label` listing all series values.

### Opt out

```tsx
<AreaChart data={data} accessibility={{ enabled: false }} />
```

## Performance Notes

- `resolvedLegendItems` and `computedDisplayProps` are memoized with `useMemo`
- `catColor` is stable via `useCallback` — no per-render string allocation
- AreaGroup handles D3 stacking with internal memoization
- Data morphing uses `requestAnimationFrame` + `d3.interpolateString` — no React re-renders during transition

